y Tailwind as a dependency unless the user instructs you to do so.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Node ids have been added to the code as data attributes, e.g. `data-node-id=\"1:2\"`."},{"type":"text","text":"These styles are contained in the design: Shadow/2nd: Effect(type: DROP_SHADOW, color: var(--effect-shadow-2nd), offset: (3.0237488746643066, 6.047497749328613), radius: 20, spread: 0), DS/Heading/22: Font(family: \"var(--text-font-sans)\", style: Bold, size: var(--text-size-22), weight: var(--text-weight-semibold), lineHeight: 1.2999999523162842, letterSpacing: 3), DS/Body/20/Regular: Font(family: \"var(--text-font-sans)\", style: Light, size: var(--text-size-20), weight: var(--text-weight-light), lineHeight: 1.600000023841858, letterSpacing: 1)."},{"type":"text","text":"The generated code contains image and SVG URL constants, e.g. const image = `${assetPathPrefix}/<asset file name>`, where assetPathPrefix is declared once at the top of the code and every asset URL interpolates it. These URLs are temporary download sources and expire after 7 days. Download each asset into the project with curl -L, then replace its URL in the generated code with a reference to the downloaded asset. Never use the temporary URLs as runtime image sources."}],"structuredContent":null,"isError":false}